>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Interactively reviewed graph. Ru–N–O 174.60°, N–O 1.16773 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.8211. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +2 and total charge +0. Terminal ligand identity, the remaining graph and charge balance were checked; The original M–N–O angle, M–N and N–O distances, and WBO agree with documented NO⁺ controls matched by metal, formal state, NO count and ligand class. Localized 12 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 39 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 34 nonmetal covalent bonds: 33 within range, 0 outside range and 1 with sparse controls. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

